Here is a Java solution that uses a loop to check if the given integer n is a power of three:

```java
public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }

        while (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3;
        }

        return n == 1;
    }
}
```

Alternatively, you can solve this problem without using loops or recursion. The idea is to find the maximum power of 3 that can be represented as a 32-bit signed integer, and then check if n is a divisor of this maximum power of 3:

```java
public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        return n > 0 && 1162261467 % n == 0;
    }
}
```
In this solution, 1162261467 is 3^19, which is the largest power of 3 that can be represented as a 32-bit signed integer. If n is a power of 3, then it must be a divisor of 3^19.

